## --- NuGet package cache (project-local, per nuget.config) ---
## Same role as node_modules -- fully reproducible from .csproj + restore,
## never belongs in version control. Pattern is recursive in case the cache
## folder ends up nested under a different project later.
**/.nuget/packages/
packages/

## --- Build output ---
bin/
obj/
out/
publish/

## --- .env / secrets ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
appsettings.Development.json
appsettings.Production.json
appsettings.Local.json
*.pfx
*.key

## --- Logs ---
logs/
*.log

## --- User/machine-specific ---
*.user
*.suo
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates
.vs/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.code-workspace

## --- ASP.NET Core Data Protection keys (dev, unencrypted at rest) ---
## These are the "keys will not be encrypted at rest" warning you saw in
## the logs -- machine-local, never portable, must never be committed.
**/DataProtection-Keys/

## --- Test results / coverage ---
TestResults/
coverage/
*.trx

## --- OS junk ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

## --- Nix (if you generate a local dev shell result) ---
result
result-*
